{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180364-protean-2-advice-rquest","id":1180364,"title":"Protean 2 advice rquest.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-29T00:47:58-08:00","id":1180364,"title":"Protean 2 advice rquest.","content":"are these adaptations OP(well mortals are lost against a Protean 2, Resilience 2 vampire anyway if they are not a swat crew):<br /> -Hunter pelt: +2 armor against mundane weapons<br /> -Feline sinew: +1 Dex or Wits (or both, result is meant to be +1 defense)<br /> (This keyboard lacks a question mark key)<br /> Advice, criticism, opinions, your own custom adaptations(the latter one only if generosity compels you) are welcome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T03:26:44-08:00","id":1180373,"title":"","content":"How I would do them:<br /> <br /> Hunter Pelt: Straight armor modifications lean a bit too close to Resilience for my taste.<br /> <br /> Feline Sinew becomes &quot;Feral Reflexes&quot;: use the highest of Dex or Wits to calculate Defense (as animals do)<br /> <br /> Poison glands: Claw/Bite attacks cause the Sick or Poisoned Tilt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T07:38:14-08:00","id":1181394,"title":"","content":"Hunter Pelt can maybe work if it counts as and does't stack with mundane armor. Even then, I would do no more than 1/0 or 2/0. Also may only be effective on attacks that are bashing to vampires.<br /> <br /> It also needs tp be masquerade breaking in appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 02-01-2018, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T05:58:43-08:00","id":1186265,"title":"","content":"Yes I was thinking of some short rough fur, so like claws breaks masquerade, and I thought of mundane as &quot;it does only bashing to vampires&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T16:22:22-08:00","id":1186465,"title":"","content":"Most things do bashing to vampires but I would allow some low amount of armor if you do have Resilience or some low strength boost if you Vigor, Def with Celerity, Stealth with Obf etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T02:36:46-08:00","id":1186595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180364-protean-2-advice-rquest?p=1186465#post1186465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most things do bashing to vampires but I would allow some low amount of armor if you do have Resilience or some low strength boost if you Vigor, Def with Celerity, Stealth with Obf etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>These would be Devotions. Not Predatory Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:05:29-08:00","id":1186622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180364-protean-2-advice-rquest?p=1186465#post1186465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most things do bashing to vampires but I would allow some low amount of armor if you do have Resilience or some low strength boost if you Vigor, Def with Celerity, Stealth with Obf etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say you could get those bonuses from different predatory aspects, no need to get other disciplines involved, but if you do i agree with Tessie, that would be devotions.<br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Chromatophore cells: your skin has transmuted into colour-changing cells akin to those found in certain cephalopods. This can change the pigment of your skin to blend into the environment better As long as you stick to walls or like things you could blend into you get a Rote action on mundane stealth rolls.<br /> <br /> (this might be an unnatural aspect) Muscular body: by converting some of your bone structure and the skin into muscle mass that's filled with vitae lets you increase your effective strength as if you spent a single blood point on physical intensity as long as this aspect is in use, effectively giving you +2 for most strength rolls.<br /> <br /> Feral Reflexes: Some animals have perceptions for reflexes and has more energy stored in their reflex muscles and sinew that far exceeds that of ordinary humans. By forming muscles, sinew and nerves and let the powers of the beast take care of reactions instead of the man the vampire gets to use the higher of dex or wits for calculating Def. Also if you're aware of your attacker you can keep your def against firearms up to dots in Protean(+ celerity)<br /> <br /> Pelt and skin of the wild; skin thickens and hardens more to hide then soft human skin and thick fur covers it, providing some protection against mundane weapons and arms and gives you an effective armour rating of 2/0 against mundane attacks that would normally inflict bashing damage to the vampire, however pelt is easily flammable so treat any fire damage the vampire suffers as one step higher on the damage chart. Also, you're burning if you suffer a single point of fire damage, see Hurt locker for Burning tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:08:39-08:00","id":1186649,"title":"","content":"The firearms part of Feral Reflexes is a bit much. Also, if you can't get the bonus in the actual animal forms, I don't think it should be granted by Predatory Aspects. That's the stuff for Unnatural Aspects, Devotions, or even Merits.<br /> <br /> I actually have an example of the latter:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Beastly Alacrity (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Riding the Wave \u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The vampire taps into the Beast and reacts with the speed of an animal. Use the higher of Wits and Dexterity when calculating Defense while in Frenzy or Riding the Wave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:53:37-08:00","id":1186662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180364-protean-2-advice-rquest?p=1186649#post1186649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The firearms part of Feral Reflexes is a bit much. Also, if you can't get the bonus in the actual animal forms, I don't think it should be granted by Predatory Aspects. That's the stuff for Unnatural Aspects, Devotions, or even Merits.<br /> <br /> I actually have an example of the latter:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Beastly Alacrity (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Riding the Wave \u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The vampire taps into the Beast and reacts with the speed of an animal. Use the higher of Wits and Dexterity when calculating Defense while in Frenzy or Riding the Wave.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can't disagree more actually. Using the higher value is usually pretty worthless, especially compared to the things protean 2 cab give you by RAW. Letting you keep some of your defense vs firearms doesn't sound that OP. Quickened sight is 1 exp and gives you full def vs firearms. (Almost ) every werewolf form lets you keep it and a fair bit of the mage armors let you keep it. So letting you keep 2-5 defense vs firearms, not increasing seems fairly okay to my ears. That is if you have defense and it's actually high enough you keep some of it. <br /> And don't getting bonuses from animal form is also null and void, quadrupedal animals don't get double jump distance whereas the protean power does indeed. <br /> But if it's still to strong or unnatural it could always be a unnatural aspect on protean 4. ^_^ <br /> <br /> Paying 3 exp with a preq to use higher wit/dex def in frenzy is just under-performing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:59:23-08:00","id":1186666,"title":"","content":"I didn't write it. I also think it's way too expensive. But in any case, Predatory Aspects are supposed to be based on mundane animals, and they certainly don't have any Defense against firearms. Werewolves and Mage Shield is extremely supernatural. And even in the case of werewolves they don't receive Defense against firearms in their two mostly mundane forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T08:07:24-08:00","id":1186667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180364-protean-2-advice-rquest?p=1186666#post1186666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't write it. I also think it's way too expensive. But in any case, Predatory Aspects are supposed to be based on mundane animals, and they certainly don't have any Defense against firearms. Werewolves and Mage Shield is extremely supernatural. And even in the case of werewolves they don't receive Defense against firearms in their two mostly mundane forms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay sorry about that, didn't recognize it from anywhere so i assumed that. Yes that's true though. Though i don't see anything wrong with letting you keep a few dots worth of defense against firearms. But i agree with your argument actually and it does probably make more sense as a protean 4 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}